# agent-mem worker environment — template.
#
# Copy to `.env` next to this file (same dir as docker-compose.yml) and fill in
# real values. `.env` is gitignored; NEVER commit real secrets anywhere in the
# repository, including here — placeholders only.
#
# ── DB-backed settings do NOT live here ─────────────────────────────────────
# 16 settings are stored in the Postgres `settings` table and edited via the
# dashboard, not from env: api_key, llm_gateway_url, llm_gateway_api_key,
# llm_hourly_call_cap, machine_id, sync_enabled, sync_url, sync_interval,
# context_observations, context_full_count, context_session_count, log_level,
# allowed_projects, ignored_projects, gemini_embedding_dims, public_base_url,
# skip_tools. That split is exactly what made the 2026-08-12 migration outage
# invisible: DB-backed settings survived the move, env-only credentials did not,
# and jobs kept "succeeding" without them. Env still takes final precedence over
# the DB (ApplyEnv runs after ApplyDBSettings), so anything set here wins.
#
# Marking: # REQUIRED = hub needs it to function. # OPTIONAL = has a sane
# default or is unused on this deployment; safe to leave commented out.

# ─── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port the worker HTTP API listens on. Default 34567. OPTIONAL.
#AGENT_MEM_WORKER_PORT=34567

# Data directory for local state. Defaults to ~/.agent-mem. OPTIONAL.
#AGENT_MEM_DATA_DIR=

# DATABASE_URL is NOT read from this file: docker-compose.yml injects it under
# `environment:` (postgres service name inside the compose network), and values
# there win over env_file by design. Leave it unset here.

# ─── Slack ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED. Bot user OAuth token (xoxb-…) for conversations.list/users.list/
# usergroups.list/chat.postMessage and Slack backfills. Its absence is why
# refresh_slack_channels failed fatally after the 2026-08-12 move.
AGENT_MEM_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-placeholder-replace-me

# REQUIRED. Slack member id (U…) of the default DM recipient: watch-channel
# alerts, hourly monitor reports, and hot-topic fallback notifications.
AGENT_MEM_SLACK_DM_USER=UPLACEHOLDER000

# ─── Jira ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED. Atlassian account email for Basic auth.
AGENT_MEM_JIRA_EMAIL=you@example.com

# REQUIRED. Jira API token (id.atlassian.com → Security → API tokens).
AGENT_MEM_JIRA_TOKEN=placeholder-jira-token

# REQUIRED. Site root, no trailing slash (refresh_jira_board fails closed
# without it). Example: https://example.atlassian.net
AGENT_MEM_JIRA_BASE_URL=https://example.atlassian.net

# ─── GitHub ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED. Personal access token for PR/issue fetchers and describe_attachment.
AGENT_MEM_GH_TOKEN=placeholder-gh-token

# REQUIRED. Site root, e.g. https://example.atlassian.net (no default).
AGENT_MEM_CF_BASE_URL=https://example.atlassian.net

# ─── Job routing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which target_runner values this worker will claim. The claim query matches
# target_runner IN ('any', $THIS). Historically 'vps' meant "the machine holding
# the Slack/Jira credentials"; since 2026-08-12 that machine is the payments Mac
# mini. Set this to 'vps' on the hub so the ~641 rows pinned to 'vps' remain
# claimable. Renaming this value is tracked in agent-mem-zn0.
AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RUNNER=vps

# ─── GitHub base URL (enterprise only) ───────────────────────────────────────

# OPTIONAL. Defaults to https://api.github.com.
#AGENT_MEM_GH_BASE_URL=

# ─── PagerDuty — UNSUPPORTED on this hub (zero nodes) ────────────────────────
# The fetcher exists but graph.nodes holds no pagerduty rows. Do not add
# credentials until a PagerDuty source actually exists.

# OPTIONAL. Defaults to https://api.pagerduty.com.
#AGENT_MEM_PAGERDUTY_TOKEN=
#AGENT_MEM_PAGERDUTY_BASE_URL=

# ─── Datadog — UNSUPPORTED on this hub (zero nodes) ──────────────────────────
# Same story as PagerDuty: fetchers exist, nothing reaches them.

# OPTIONAL.
#AGENT_MEM_DATADOG_API_KEY=
#AGENT_MEM_DATADOG_APP_KEY=
# Defaults to https://api.datadoghq.com.
#AGENT_MEM_DATADOG_BASE_URL=

# ─── Sentry — UNSUPPORTED on this hub (zero nodes) ───────────────────────────

# OPTIONAL.
#AGENT_MEM_SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Defaults to https://sentry.io.
#AGENT_MEM_SENTRY_BASE_URL=
#AGENT_MEM_SENTRY_ORG=

# ─── Google Workspace — UNSUPPORTED (needs a volume mount) ───────────────────
# UNSUPPORTED (needs a volume mount): AGENT_MEM_GWS_SERVICE_KEY_PATH must point
# at a service-account JSON mounted INTO the container, which is a bigger
# compose change (78 gws_doc nodes today). Not wired up in this round.

#AGENT_MEM_GWS_SERVICE_KEY_PATH=

# ─── Wego Hub ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Token for the internal Wego Hub integration (describe_attachment auth).
# Set if any wego_hub attachments are ingested; otherwise leave unset. OPTIONAL.
#AGENT_MEM_WEGOHUB_TOKEN=
# Base URL for the Wego Hub API. OPTIONAL.
#AGENT_MEM_WEGOHUB_BASE_URL=

# ─── Per-source concurrency caps ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL. All have sane defaults (config.go defaults(): Slack 5, Jira 5,
# GitHub 10, Confluence 5, PagerDuty 3, Datadog 3, Sentry 5, GWS 5, Gemini 4);
# an unset var is harmless. Do not raise these casually — they throttle calls
# against shared third-party APIs.

#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_SLACK=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_JIRA=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_GITHUB=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_CONFLUENCE=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_PAGERDUTY=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_DATADOG=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_SENTRY=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_GWS=
#AGENT_MEM_GRAPH_RATE_GEMINI=

# ─── LLM gateway / misc env overrides (normally leave unset) ─────────────────
# These are DB-backed settings first (see header); env overrides exist but the
# values belong in the `settings` table. Listed for completeness because
# config.go reads them.

#AGENT_MEM_LLM_GATEWAY_URL=
#AGENT_MEM_LLM_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
#AGENT_MEM_GEMINI_EMBEDDING_DIMS=
#AGENT_MEM_CONTEXT_OBSERVATIONS=
#AGENT_MEM_CONTEXT_FULL_COUNT=
#AGENT_MEM_CONTEXT_SESSION_COUNT=
#AGENT_MEM_SKIP_TOOLS=
#AGENT_MEM_ALLOWED_PROJECTS=
#AGENT_MEM_IGNORED_PROJECTS=
#AGENT_MEM_LOG_LEVEL=
#AGENT_MEM_SYNC_ENABLED=
#AGENT_MEM_SYNC_URL=
#AGENT_MEM_SYNC_INTERVAL=
#AGENT_MEM_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
#AGENT_MEM_API_KEY=
#AGENT_MEM_MACHINE_ID=

# Postgres password used BY COMPOSE ONLY (interpolated into POSTGRES_PASSWORD
# and the worker's DATABASE_URL). Not read by config.go. Change from the
# default before exposing postgres beyond localhost.
#AGENT_MEM_PG_PASSWORD=
